diagnosis_text:
A topology-wide reachability test (Phase 1) found 0% packet loss on both the pc1→pc2 and pc2→pc1 paths. All four subsequent diagnostic phases returned clean results. The BGP session between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) is currently Established and has been continuously Established since the lab started at 22:29:08 — the BGP neighbor counters show exactly 1 connection established and 0 dropped on both sides, with 0 Notification messages exchanged in either direction. The FRR log on both routers contains only the expected initial session bring-up (OPEN/UPDATE at 22:29:08) followed by regular 60-second KEEPALIVE exchanges through to the present; there are no IDLE, ACTIVE, or session-reset entries anywhere in the log. No process, cron job, or script that could periodically disrupt the BGP daemon or the underlying TCP session exists on either router. Interface statistics on the router1-eth0 ↔ router2-eth0 link show zero carrier changes, zero errors, and zero drops since boot. BGP timers are the standard defaults (hold=180 s, keepalive=60 s), with no BFD or password misconfiguration that could trigger spurious resets. In short, every mechanism that would be required to produce an intermittent BGP session flap is absent, and the historical logs contain no trace of such an event having occurred. The helpdesk ticket's claim of repeating BGP session resets is unconfirmed by direct evidence; the network is operating normally.
=== END ===